  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I recently found that voices of all other players completely turn off for a period of time when players are in stations on a vehicle that accelerates. This seems to happen at the same time for all players in the vehicle. I observed it consistently occurring when any driving player pressed buttons that \"Hop\" or \"Boost\" the vehicle (which differ from normal wheel-collider acceleration by applying direct force to the vehicle rigidbody). This seemed to happen regardless of individual player's connection quality. At first I thought this was the players \"out-running\" the sound itself, (which seems absurd), but it appeared to only happen during and immediately after acceleration regardless of the vehicle's actual speed. This was observed in a test world that uses origin point shifting and some avatar scaling stuff (might be related) and it also seemed to happen at any distance from origin (0m - 5000m).",
